1
00:00:06,172 --> 00:00:09,676
[quiet, tense music playing]

2
00:00:13,096 --> 00:00:14,472
[Josh, anxiously] Oh man.

3
00:00:19,310 --> 00:00:22,313
It's not too bad.
I'll fix it in a couple of days.

4
00:00:23,023 --> 00:00:25,900
But it begs the question, why should I?

5
00:00:25,984 --> 00:00:28,361
Why were you in a car accident?
Why is this a secret?

6
00:00:28,445 --> 00:00:29,863
I can't tell you.

7
00:00:29,946 --> 00:00:32,449
It's not because I don't want to,
it's just…

8
00:00:34,951 --> 00:00:36,286
It's not mine to tell.

9
00:00:36,369 --> 00:00:37,579
-Are you safe?
-Yes.

10
00:00:38,788 --> 00:00:39,789
Is he in trouble?

11
00:00:39,873 --> 00:00:42,417
He will be
if anyone finds out about this accident.

12
00:00:42,500 --> 00:00:45,211
-Are you asking me for help or is he?
-Cam, I am.

13
00:00:45,712 --> 00:00:47,922
And I wouldn't be asking you
if it wasn't important.

14
00:00:50,425 --> 00:00:52,177
But you don't owe me anything.

15
00:00:54,429 --> 00:00:55,680
Kind of do.

16
00:00:56,723 --> 00:00:58,266
I'll take care of it.

17
00:00:59,392 --> 00:01:00,810
[Teagan whispers] Thank you.

18
00:01:00,894 --> 00:01:03,313
But next time,
I'm not bailing out your shitty boyfriend.

19
00:01:03,396 --> 00:01:04,898
He's not my boyfriend.

20
00:01:04,981 --> 00:01:07,901
No, I'm just a shitty friend.

21
00:01:08,651 --> 00:01:11,237
Cam, whatever it costs, I'll cover it.

22
00:01:11,321 --> 00:01:12,447
It's a favor for Teagan.

23
00:01:13,323 --> 00:01:14,741
Right, well…

24
00:01:16,576 --> 00:01:17,827
I won't forget this.

25
00:01:19,454 --> 00:01:21,456
[intriguing music playing]

26
00:01:25,376 --> 00:01:31,299
[upbeat music playing]

27
00:01:31,382 --> 00:01:33,885
[high-energy music playing]

28
00:01:33,968 --> 00:01:35,220
And legs!

29
00:01:36,179 --> 00:01:41,935
Come on, push! Last practice
before the Haverford Cup, come on!

30
00:01:44,312 --> 00:01:45,188
Let's go!

31
00:01:51,194 --> 00:01:53,613
This race is the big one.

32
00:01:56,991 --> 00:01:59,035
Way to bring it, Josh. Come on!

33
00:01:59,119 --> 00:02:02,705
{\an8}-Great, keep it high, slow into slings.
-[Lana] Great job, boys.

34
00:02:02,789 --> 00:02:04,124
[Hayden] Good hustle.

35
00:02:04,207 --> 00:02:05,542
{\an8}Man, practice today was sick.

36
00:02:05,625 --> 00:02:07,877
{\an8}Josh kept the ratio tight.
Nice work, guys.

37
00:02:07,961 --> 00:02:11,005
{\an8}Looking good out there, everyone.
Well done.

38
00:02:11,089 --> 00:02:13,007
{\an8}Josh, keep it up.
You're earning your keep.

39
00:02:13,091 --> 00:02:15,593
{\an8}And perfect time to bring your A game,

40
00:02:15,677 --> 00:02:19,514
{\an8}because Easton only hosts
the Haverford Cup once every five years.

41
00:02:19,597 --> 00:02:22,100
-You think we have a chance?
-[Hayden] Not gonna sugarcoat it.

42
00:02:22,183 --> 00:02:23,726
Competition's gonna be brutal.

43
00:02:23,810 --> 00:02:27,105
Westvale, Vic City, Claremont,
only the best of the best.

44
00:02:27,188 --> 00:02:31,109
-But who won at the Head of the Laurence?
-[team] We did.

45
00:02:31,192 --> 00:02:32,861
Who won at the Head of the Laurence?

46
00:02:32,944 --> 00:02:34,195
-[louder] We did!
-Damn right.

47
00:02:34,279 --> 00:02:35,697
-And was it a fluke?
-No!

48
00:02:35,780 --> 00:02:37,407
No! And now,

49
00:02:37,490 --> 00:02:40,410
now you have a shot
at medaling at the Haverford Cup.

50
00:02:40,493 --> 00:02:44,873
So go get changed and let's kick some ass
out on the water tomorrow.

51
00:02:44,956 --> 00:02:47,667
Quaid, take us out, big man!

52
00:02:48,376 --> 00:02:50,420
[imitating air horn]

53
00:02:50,503 --> 00:02:52,213
[all cheering]

54
00:02:53,047 --> 00:02:56,342
Okay, there's five boats in our heat,
so if we beat two, we could get bronze.

55
00:02:56,426 --> 00:03:00,221
Except everyone we're up against
has already taken the cup home before.

56
00:03:03,266 --> 00:03:04,184
What's going on?

57
00:03:05,226 --> 00:03:07,520
Baloo says Josh has something to tell us.

58
00:03:09,480 --> 00:03:12,066
[tense music playing]

59
00:03:15,236 --> 00:03:16,654
Well, what is it?

60
00:03:23,578 --> 00:03:25,705
I'm the reason we lost
the Head of the Harbor regatta.

61
00:03:27,123 --> 00:03:28,249
I sabotaged the oar.

62
00:03:29,125 --> 00:03:30,376
What the hell?

63
00:03:30,460 --> 00:03:33,171
-What?
-You made us lose? Why?

64
00:03:33,254 --> 00:03:34,714
[Perry] How could you do that?

65
00:03:34,797 --> 00:03:35,840
[Noah] You lied to us?

66
00:03:35,924 --> 00:03:37,508
[Baloo] Yeah, and he was gonna keep lying.

67
00:03:38,468 --> 00:03:39,969
[Noah] Well, answer us.

68
00:03:43,556 --> 00:03:44,766
He choked.

69
00:03:49,520 --> 00:03:50,521
You're right.

70
00:03:51,022 --> 00:03:53,358
I sabotaged my own oar
to get out of the race.

71
00:03:53,441 --> 00:03:55,735
So what about Baloo's Westvale boyfriend?

72
00:03:55,818 --> 00:03:58,488
No, Logan had nothing to do with it.

73
00:03:58,571 --> 00:04:01,491
I let him take the blame
because I was a coward.

74
00:04:02,909 --> 00:04:05,703
So you got scared and bailed.
Is that gonna happen again tomorrow?

75
00:04:05,787 --> 00:04:06,704
No.

76
00:04:07,872 --> 00:04:12,669
Why should we believe that?
Guys, you need somebody you can count on.

77
00:04:13,419 --> 00:04:18,591
Now, all you gotta do
is tell Coach that you want me in stroke.

78
00:04:18,675 --> 00:04:19,842
Guys, look,

79
00:04:20,343 --> 00:04:24,555
I know trusting me after what I did
is a big ask,

80
00:04:24,639 --> 00:04:26,057
but I can get us to the podium.

81
00:04:28,434 --> 00:04:29,769
Look, Josh messed up,

82
00:04:29,852 --> 00:04:33,523
but practice today was phenomenal.
He's our best shot at medaling.

83
00:04:34,649 --> 00:04:35,858
I can't row for him.

84
00:04:46,327 --> 00:04:50,373
He owned up to it.
That's gotta count for something.

85
00:04:51,791 --> 00:04:54,168
Now, Ryder was stroke when we won.

86
00:04:54,252 --> 00:04:56,629
Teagan won that race.

87
00:04:59,382 --> 00:05:01,801
But it was a winning boat.

88
00:05:08,641 --> 00:05:12,020
Okay, well, you're the tiebreaker, Cam.
Who gets your vote?

89
00:05:13,187 --> 00:05:14,647
Neither of you.

90
00:05:15,523 --> 00:05:17,525
I'm gonna sit this one out, thanks.

91
00:05:19,569 --> 00:05:20,570
[Teagan] Cam.

92
00:05:27,493 --> 00:05:28,703
Didn't think you had it in you.

93
00:05:30,038 --> 00:05:31,122
To own it like that.

94
00:05:31,956 --> 00:05:35,668
Me neither. I'm really sorry, Baloo.

95
00:05:35,752 --> 00:05:39,130
And I'm gonna DM Logan everything
and tell him what happened.

96
00:05:41,883 --> 00:05:43,092
Still not getting my vote.

97
00:05:44,677 --> 00:05:45,887
Fair.

98
00:05:46,804 --> 00:05:49,766
[melancholy music playing]

99
00:05:53,019 --> 00:05:56,397
[vehicle approaching]

100
00:05:57,899 --> 00:05:58,941
[car door opens]

101
00:06:00,526 --> 00:06:02,862
-Juliet.
-I was just seeing if Teagan was home.

102
00:06:02,945 --> 00:06:04,614
-I'll head out.
-Hey.

103
00:06:06,491 --> 00:06:07,450
Are you okay?

104
00:06:09,619 --> 00:06:12,580
My mom canceled
my flight home for Christmas.

105
00:06:12,663 --> 00:06:14,874
She thinks it's better
I stay until spring break.

106
00:06:14,957 --> 00:06:17,168
-Why?
-She didn't say.

107
00:06:17,835 --> 00:06:20,546
I burn a car, they send a new one.

108
00:06:20,630 --> 00:06:23,383
I fake my own kidnapping,
they send an extraction team.

109
00:06:24,342 --> 00:06:26,552
When will they ever just send themselves?

110
00:06:27,220 --> 00:06:29,806
There is only one thing left to do.

111
00:06:30,765 --> 00:06:31,599
Emancipate.

112
00:06:31,682 --> 00:06:33,393
Or maybe just talk to them.

113
00:06:34,685 --> 00:06:37,688
-Or--
-I need to get a job and a place to stay.

114
00:06:37,772 --> 00:06:42,151
And… something else.
I got bored of the AI summary.

115
00:06:42,235 --> 00:06:43,778
[knocking on door]

116
00:06:50,159 --> 00:06:51,160
[door opens]

117
00:06:53,121 --> 00:06:54,455
[Ella] Richard Regis?

118
00:06:54,539 --> 00:06:56,624
[Richard] Hi, Ella. Can we talk?

119
00:06:59,919 --> 00:07:04,215
As you know, my father, Viktor,
is president of Easton's rowing committee.

120
00:07:04,298 --> 00:07:07,009
He's hosting
the Haverford Cup viewing party tomorrow.

121
00:07:07,093 --> 00:07:10,471
It's a very important gathering,
and our party planner just quit.

122
00:07:10,555 --> 00:07:12,056
Not interested.

123
00:07:12,140 --> 00:07:13,850
Wait, let's hear him out.

124
00:07:13,933 --> 00:07:16,185
[intriguing music playing]

125
00:07:16,269 --> 00:07:19,355
Viktor mentioned
the party you threw for Josh.

126
00:07:19,439 --> 00:07:21,858
-The one you fired me from.
-He wants you to take over.

127
00:07:21,941 --> 00:07:23,401
Hm.

128
00:07:25,278 --> 00:07:26,988
I'll make it worth your while.

129
00:07:27,071 --> 00:07:29,657
How much do you make
at the Crab Shack in a year? 50K?

130
00:07:30,825 --> 00:07:33,536
Surprisingly accurate
for someone wearing an ascot.

131
00:07:33,619 --> 00:07:36,247
I'll double it. For one day's work.

132
00:07:37,665 --> 00:07:41,335
What about tripling it
and adding a hospitality coordinator?

133
00:07:41,419 --> 00:07:44,088
I'm sorry. Who are you?

134
00:07:44,172 --> 00:07:46,048
The hospitality coordinator.

135
00:07:46,674 --> 00:07:48,384
-Huh.
-Well?

136
00:07:51,220 --> 00:07:52,221
Done.

137
00:07:58,686 --> 00:07:59,520
[door closes]

138
00:07:59,604 --> 00:08:02,023
-What?
-Looks like we got a job.

139
00:08:03,941 --> 00:08:05,151
Should've seen practice this morning.

140
00:08:05,234 --> 00:08:07,778
I think you're gonna be very happy
at the race tomorrow.

141
00:08:07,862 --> 00:08:08,863
Well, good to hear it.

142
00:08:08,946 --> 00:08:11,741
I don't wanna jinx it,
but there might be a medal in our future.

143
00:08:11,824 --> 00:08:12,742
[laughs]

144
00:08:13,493 --> 00:08:15,244
-Everything all right?
-No.

145
00:08:15,328 --> 00:08:19,415
The Cambridge Racing Committee
conducted a full inspection of the erg

146
00:08:19,499 --> 00:08:22,126
that Teagan and Cam raced on last week.

147
00:08:22,210 --> 00:08:24,795
-And what'd they find?
-Blister tape in the flywheel.

148
00:08:24,879 --> 00:08:28,424
Okay, well, most rowers use blister tape
to protect their hands.

149
00:08:28,508 --> 00:08:31,135
-I can see how some'd get in the rigging.
-It wasn't an accident.

150
00:08:31,219 --> 00:08:32,094
Meaning?

151
00:08:32,178 --> 00:08:34,180
The machine was tampered with.

152
00:08:34,263 --> 00:08:36,098
And after the equipment check,

153
00:08:36,182 --> 00:08:40,645
the only people who came near that
particular machine were Teagan and Cam.

154
00:08:40,728 --> 00:08:42,813
That's a very serious accusation.

155
00:08:42,897 --> 00:08:43,940
Yes, it is.

156
00:08:44,023 --> 00:08:47,985
Since it only affected our rowers,
I was able to convince the committee

157
00:08:48,069 --> 00:08:49,737
to let us deal with it internally.

158
00:08:49,820 --> 00:08:52,365
But you need to find out
whether it was Teagan or Cam

159
00:08:52,448 --> 00:08:54,158
who tampered with the machine.

160
00:08:54,867 --> 00:08:55,993
And pull them from the boat.

161
00:08:56,077 --> 00:08:58,120
[tense music playing]

162
00:08:58,204 --> 00:09:00,039
You cannot ask me to do that.

163
00:09:00,122 --> 00:09:02,500
I want to win as much as anyone.

164
00:09:03,000 --> 00:09:06,587
But if the committee finds out
that we did not deal with this properly,

165
00:09:06,671 --> 00:09:08,381
Easton will be barred from rowing.

166
00:09:15,012 --> 00:09:18,474
[gloomy music playing]

167
00:09:30,570 --> 00:09:32,113
[sinister music playing]

168
00:09:40,413 --> 00:09:41,872
-[quietly] Dad?
-Hi, Teagan.

169
00:09:41,956 --> 00:09:43,374
How are you here?

170
00:09:43,457 --> 00:09:45,001
I wanted to see you row.

171
00:09:45,501 --> 00:09:47,420
I hear you're a coxswain now.

172
00:09:50,381 --> 00:09:51,382
Let's talk.

173
00:09:54,802 --> 00:09:57,013
After I found out the money was misspent,

174
00:09:57,096 --> 00:09:58,889
I was trying to make everything right.

175
00:09:58,973 --> 00:10:01,392
But then the FBI got wind,
and I ran out of time.

176
00:10:01,475 --> 00:10:02,852
So you left.

177
00:10:02,935 --> 00:10:05,271
-I thought about you every day.
-That doesn't make it better.

178
00:10:05,354 --> 00:10:09,567
That just means that you decided every day
not to be here with us.

179
00:10:10,067 --> 00:10:11,652
I wasn't just running away.

180
00:10:11,736 --> 00:10:15,698
-I was trying to fix things.
-Fix things? Gosh.

181
00:10:17,158 --> 00:10:20,745
I have this now.
It's evidence of everything that we did.

182
00:10:20,828 --> 00:10:24,540
I can sell this for enough money
to set you and your mom up properly.

183
00:10:24,624 --> 00:10:26,083
I don't want that.

184
00:10:26,167 --> 00:10:30,588
You and your mom are both so stubborn,
you know that?

185
00:10:30,671 --> 00:10:32,757
Why won't you two take the money?

186
00:10:32,840 --> 00:10:34,508
I'm trying to help you.

187
00:10:36,802 --> 00:10:39,138
Hold on, what do you mean? Did you see…

188
00:10:39,221 --> 00:10:40,598
Did you see Mom?

189
00:10:43,517 --> 00:10:45,811
Mom knew you were here,
and she didn't tell me?

190
00:10:45,895 --> 00:10:47,980
She didn't want you to get hurt.

191
00:10:49,273 --> 00:10:50,274
Don't be mad at her.

192
00:10:50,358 --> 00:10:52,777
I can't believe this.
I'm gonna be late. I have to go.

193
00:10:52,860 --> 00:10:56,238
Wait, Teag. If I'd stayed, the FBI
would've put me in prison for 20 years--

194
00:10:56,322 --> 00:10:58,741
At least I would've known where you were!

195
00:10:58,824 --> 00:11:01,035
Okay? I could've talked to you!

196
00:11:01,535 --> 00:11:02,995
Don't you get it?

197
00:11:03,079 --> 00:11:06,957
There's only ever been one person
who has kept my dad away,

198
00:11:07,041 --> 00:11:08,250
and that's you!

199
00:11:16,008 --> 00:11:19,428
[upbeat, rousing music playing]

200
00:11:19,512 --> 00:11:23,057
[announcer] All rowers to the docks.
The race will be starting shortly.

201
00:11:32,191 --> 00:11:34,694
Rowing is such an exciting sport.

202
00:11:35,611 --> 00:11:40,157
Have you ever thought about
expanding Easton's rowing program?

203
00:11:40,658 --> 00:11:43,452
Well, we'd love to,
but it's always a challenge

204
00:11:43,536 --> 00:11:46,288
to find enough interest or funding.

205
00:11:46,372 --> 00:11:47,707
It's funny you say that.

206
00:11:51,836 --> 00:11:54,046
This is definitely
the fanciest I've ever looked

207
00:11:54,130 --> 00:11:55,631
to watch a high school sporting event.

208
00:11:55,715 --> 00:11:58,134
Apparently it's tradition
at the Haverford Cup.

209
00:11:58,217 --> 00:12:00,845
You dress like you're going
to the Kentucky Derby.

210
00:12:01,429 --> 00:12:05,266
This one, circulate appetizers. This one,
keep the charcuterie board loaded.

211
00:12:05,349 --> 00:12:08,602
This one, champagne.
Keep it flowing, like the Mississippi.

212
00:12:09,186 --> 00:12:10,438
You're a natural.

213
00:12:10,521 --> 00:12:12,690
-I've got dictator energy.
-[Ella giggles]

214
00:12:14,734 --> 00:12:16,944
[Noah] Just let it go.
We have to race in 20 minutes.

215
00:12:17,027 --> 00:12:19,280
We can't get in the boat
until there's a majority.

216
00:12:20,448 --> 00:12:21,949
You guys seriously wanna row for Josh?

217
00:12:22,032 --> 00:12:23,117
-We do.
-I do.

218
00:12:26,579 --> 00:12:28,456
What are you doing?
Why aren't you on the tarmac?

219
00:12:28,539 --> 00:12:30,499
Are you, Noah, or Perry
gonna switch sides?

220
00:12:30,583 --> 00:12:32,084
You're all still fighting about this?

221
00:12:32,168 --> 00:12:34,837
Guys, come on.
We actually have a shot at medaling.

222
00:12:34,920 --> 00:12:38,257
We're not tanking this opportunity
because of some stupid team spat.

223
00:12:38,340 --> 00:12:40,843
Josh screwed the team,
so the team gets to decide

224
00:12:40,926 --> 00:12:42,094
whether or not to row for him.

225
00:12:42,178 --> 00:12:44,680
Stroke seat is Coach's choice.

226
00:12:44,764 --> 00:12:47,057
Except if everyone
refuses to row for someone.

227
00:12:47,850 --> 00:12:49,143
There's nothing he can do.

228
00:12:52,146 --> 00:12:53,189
Fine.

229
00:12:53,689 --> 00:12:56,734
Then let's get a decision. Cam, over here.

230
00:12:58,819 --> 00:13:00,613
She seems mad.

231
00:13:00,696 --> 00:13:02,907
-What is going on with you?
-A lot of family stuff.

232
00:13:02,990 --> 00:13:05,659
This team is the only thing
that makes sense in my life.

233
00:13:05,743 --> 00:13:07,912
I don't need this bullshit.
Who is it gonna be, Cam?

234
00:13:07,995 --> 00:13:09,622
Teagan, there are no good options.

235
00:13:09,705 --> 00:13:12,958
You really want me to choose between
the one who bribed me or sabotaged me?

236
00:13:13,042 --> 00:13:14,919
Yes. Yes, I do. Because guess what?

237
00:13:15,002 --> 00:13:17,463
If you wanna be a leader,
this is what leadership looks like.

238
00:13:17,546 --> 00:13:21,050
Sometimes all you have are bad options,
and you have to make a choice.

239
00:13:28,390 --> 00:13:29,391
Fine.

240
00:13:32,978 --> 00:13:34,939
[suspenseful music playing]

241
00:13:36,273 --> 00:13:37,399
It's Josh.

242
00:13:41,862 --> 00:13:42,863
We good?

243
00:13:44,198 --> 00:13:45,491
I guess the crew has spoken.

244
00:13:46,492 --> 00:13:47,910
[Crabcatcher clears throat]

245
00:14:01,590 --> 00:14:04,343
Teagan, Cam. My office.

246
00:14:08,597 --> 00:14:10,182
Hey, Ryder.

247
00:14:11,475 --> 00:14:12,935
You win some, you lose some.

248
00:14:13,435 --> 00:14:14,812
I wanna win them all.

249
00:14:14,895 --> 00:14:17,189
Are we really gonna keep competing
for the rest of our lives?

250
00:14:18,023 --> 00:14:19,316
I didn't make the rules.

251
00:14:19,400 --> 00:14:21,819
Come on, if you had
a heart attack tomorrow,

252
00:14:21,902 --> 00:14:24,113
do you think stroke seat
would be the thing that matters?

253
00:14:24,196 --> 00:14:27,575
-Probably not to you since you're in it.
-It doesn't actually matter.

254
00:14:27,658 --> 00:14:29,785
Right. Like you'd ever give up stroke.

255
00:14:29,869 --> 00:14:33,038
-We used to be friends.
-You mean you used to have a sidekick.

256
00:14:33,122 --> 00:14:35,374
Hey. What can I do to make things right?

257
00:14:37,877 --> 00:14:39,128
You wanna be friends?

258
00:14:40,546 --> 00:14:41,797
Give me stroke seat.

259
00:14:42,631 --> 00:14:46,343
[sinister music playing]

260
00:14:49,847 --> 00:14:51,140
You know you don't deserve it.

261
00:14:52,975 --> 00:14:55,144
You are not the best man for the job.

262
00:14:56,186 --> 00:14:57,271
You know it.

263
00:15:04,486 --> 00:15:06,906
There. Twenty percent less ugly.

264
00:15:08,824 --> 00:15:10,034
You're not one of my servers.

265
00:15:11,368 --> 00:15:13,078
Do I know you? You seem familiar.

266
00:15:13,162 --> 00:15:15,122
I'm actually looking for someone.

267
00:15:16,457 --> 00:15:17,917
-David.
-Hey, El.

268
00:15:18,000 --> 00:15:20,377
Oh, yeah, you're Teagan's outlaw dad.

269
00:15:20,461 --> 00:15:23,005
Picture of you on the news is fire,
by the way.

270
00:15:23,088 --> 00:15:24,882
What are you doing here?

271
00:15:24,965 --> 00:15:26,467
I wanted to watch Teagan row.

272
00:15:27,426 --> 00:15:29,178
But the FBI tracked me down.

273
00:15:29,678 --> 00:15:32,014
So you came here? Oh, my God.

274
00:15:32,097 --> 00:15:35,392
Ella, I'm sorry.
I wouldn't be here if I didn't need help.

275
00:15:35,476 --> 00:15:38,270
If I can just stay out of sight
until the regatta's over,

276
00:15:38,354 --> 00:15:39,730
I can leave with the crowd.

277
00:15:39,813 --> 00:15:41,607
I can't help you, David.

278
00:15:41,690 --> 00:15:43,609
So what, are you just gonna turn me in?

279
00:15:44,193 --> 00:15:47,696
-I don't know.
-Hang on, he's Teagan's dad.

280
00:15:48,781 --> 00:15:51,158
Is he a bit of a disaster? Yes.

281
00:15:51,700 --> 00:15:53,327
Hugely embarrassing? Also yes.

282
00:15:54,203 --> 00:15:55,829
But he is here.

283
00:15:56,455 --> 00:15:59,541
He risked everything
because he wanted to see his daughter.

284
00:15:59,625 --> 00:16:00,626
He showed up.

285
00:16:01,126 --> 00:16:03,170
Which is more than I can say
for some parents.

286
00:16:10,219 --> 00:16:12,262
Put this on, keep your head down,

287
00:16:12,346 --> 00:16:14,390
and if you wanna be useful,
wash some dishes.

288
00:16:14,473 --> 00:16:15,641
Thank you, Ella.

289
00:16:15,724 --> 00:16:18,185
I'm not doing it for you.
I'm doing it for Teagan.

290
00:16:19,728 --> 00:16:22,189
"A disaster" and "hugely embarrassing"?

291
00:16:22,272 --> 00:16:23,232
Own it.

292
00:16:25,275 --> 00:16:29,571
The racing committee found tape
deliberately fed into the drive chain.

293
00:16:30,739 --> 00:16:31,824
Who was it?

294
00:16:32,658 --> 00:16:34,618
-It was me.
-No! It…

295
00:16:34,702 --> 00:16:36,078
-It was me.
-Okay, but I--

296
00:16:36,161 --> 00:16:38,580
I… I tampered with the erg.

297
00:16:38,664 --> 00:16:42,251
I used black blister tape, and I did it
knowing it would disqualify our scores.

298
00:16:42,334 --> 00:16:44,169
Teagan, why would you do that?

299
00:16:44,253 --> 00:16:47,631
I can't answer that. And neither can Cam.

300
00:16:49,842 --> 00:16:51,301
[sighs]

301
00:16:53,846 --> 00:16:55,639
Thank you for your honesty.

302
00:16:56,890 --> 00:16:57,975
You're out of the boat.

303
00:16:58,976 --> 00:17:01,395
-[Cam] But Coach, you can't--
-[Hayden] I don't have a choice.

304
00:17:01,478 --> 00:17:05,232
I'm gonna have to pull up a junior cox.
Cam, just go gather the rest of the crew.

305
00:17:14,491 --> 00:17:16,076
Let me be the one to tell them.

306
00:17:16,160 --> 00:17:17,161
Okay.

307
00:17:20,039 --> 00:17:21,040
Coach, I'm…

308
00:17:22,374 --> 00:17:24,293
I'm… I'm sorry.

309
00:17:26,545 --> 00:17:27,546
So am I.

310
00:17:38,140 --> 00:17:42,686
[melancholy music playing]

311
00:17:50,319 --> 00:17:51,361
[exhales]

312
00:18:07,753 --> 00:18:10,839
[footsteps approaching]

313
00:18:16,845 --> 00:18:18,347
Teagan, what's going on?

314
00:18:21,558 --> 00:18:23,352
I need to talk to you guys.

315
00:18:26,313 --> 00:18:27,815
Um…

316
00:18:29,983 --> 00:18:31,610
I messed up.

317
00:18:33,028 --> 00:18:37,032
I violated one of the rules
of the rowing committee, and…

318
00:18:38,158 --> 00:18:40,035
I need to withdraw from the race.

319
00:18:40,536 --> 00:18:41,537
What?

320
00:18:41,620 --> 00:18:42,621
You're not coxing?

321
00:18:42,704 --> 00:18:43,705
No.

322
00:18:44,206 --> 00:18:45,999
There's gonna be a cox
from the junior team.

323
00:18:46,083 --> 00:18:49,211
-They're gonna lead you out on the water.
-[Baloo] No, you're not leaving.

324
00:18:49,294 --> 00:18:50,671
-You can't.
-[rower] This isn't fair.

325
00:18:50,754 --> 00:18:51,588
We're gonna lose.

326
00:18:54,133 --> 00:18:55,843
You guys don't need me.

327
00:18:59,346 --> 00:19:00,973
You only need each other.

328
00:19:02,224 --> 00:19:04,393
I'm sorry I let you guys down.

329
00:19:06,311 --> 00:19:07,729
So, uh…

330
00:19:10,149 --> 00:19:11,150
[clears throat]

331
00:19:12,359 --> 00:19:14,653
Thank you, guys, really.

332
00:19:16,989 --> 00:19:19,867
I won't do it.
I won't row. Not without you.

333
00:19:19,950 --> 00:19:21,118
Cam.

334
00:19:21,201 --> 00:19:23,787
If she's out, I'm out.

335
00:19:29,585 --> 00:19:34,047
[quiet, determined music playing]

336
00:19:34,131 --> 00:19:35,132
I'm with him.

337
00:19:37,176 --> 00:19:38,844
It's not the same boat without you.

338
00:19:41,263 --> 00:19:42,431
I've got you, Big Tea.

339
00:19:44,349 --> 00:19:47,769
I'd rather lose with you
than win without you.

340
00:19:49,271 --> 00:19:52,357
"O Coxswain! My Coxswain!"

341
00:19:52,441 --> 00:19:53,483
[laughs and sobs]

342
00:19:55,277 --> 00:19:56,403
No cinephiles?

343
00:19:56,486 --> 00:19:58,739
Dude. <i>Dead Poets Society</i>.

344
00:19:59,239 --> 00:20:00,908
[Teagan laughs]

345
00:20:00,991 --> 00:20:02,201
Medals are ugly, anyway.

346
00:20:05,746 --> 00:20:07,873
We both know I never would've
come this far without you.

347
00:20:10,584 --> 00:20:12,127
Just so I'm clear,

348
00:20:12,836 --> 00:20:15,589
you all refuse to race
without Teagan as your coxswain.

349
00:20:17,925 --> 00:20:21,345
After all the hard work you put in
and being this close to a podium,

350
00:20:21,845 --> 00:20:22,804
you'd throw it all away.

351
00:20:30,270 --> 00:20:31,271
Teagan.

352
00:20:32,231 --> 00:20:33,357
You're up.

353
00:20:33,440 --> 00:20:34,441
What?

354
00:20:37,402 --> 00:20:39,279
So I'm back in the… in the boat?

355
00:20:39,363 --> 00:20:41,156
You deserve to be there with your team.

356
00:20:41,657 --> 00:20:44,451
You faced your consequences.
I'll face mine.

357
00:20:49,957 --> 00:20:52,251
-Let's go!
-[all cheering]

358
00:20:55,087 --> 00:20:56,338
Okay, let's go win a race!

359
00:20:56,421 --> 00:20:58,131
-Let's go!
-Let's go!

360
00:21:03,095 --> 00:21:04,096
Wow.

361
00:21:06,890 --> 00:21:08,308
Hey. How are you?

362
00:21:13,272 --> 00:21:14,731
Oh! Yes.

363
00:21:16,108 --> 00:21:18,902
Ryder's been speaking
with the junior national scout.

364
00:21:18,986 --> 00:21:21,363
It looks like
there's a place for him next year.

365
00:21:21,446 --> 00:21:22,447
Excellent.

366
00:21:22,531 --> 00:21:24,408
Dad. Karina.

367
00:21:24,908 --> 00:21:27,786
How are the relocation plans
to Rotterdam coming along?

368
00:21:27,869 --> 00:21:33,166
There's more pressing things to focus on,
like Ryder's winter training plans.

369
00:21:33,917 --> 00:21:36,378
Dad, this is Ella,
our fabulous party planner,

370
00:21:36,461 --> 00:21:37,796
as you requested.

371
00:21:37,879 --> 00:21:40,841
Good job, you tracked her down.
Wonderful party.

372
00:21:40,924 --> 00:21:44,678
Thank you. Best place to watch the race
is right over there.

373
00:21:50,517 --> 00:21:51,852
Where's Imogen?

374
00:21:51,935 --> 00:21:55,314
She's on a soul-searching tour
around the world.

375
00:21:56,273 --> 00:21:58,734
We haven't been the same
since Josh's birthday.

376
00:21:59,234 --> 00:22:02,070
Something tells me
you have something to do with that.

377
00:22:02,696 --> 00:22:03,697
No.

378
00:22:04,239 --> 00:22:07,326
I just told her to see people
for who they really are.

379
00:22:09,703 --> 00:22:12,748
There are binoculars on the table
to help see the race.

380
00:22:14,541 --> 00:22:16,293
[Announcer] Welcome, rowers.

381
00:22:18,086 --> 00:22:20,964
<i>Teams for race four,</i>
<i>make your way to the starting line.</i>

382
00:22:33,685 --> 00:22:36,855
[Josh] Yo, Cam. You got a sec?

383
00:22:37,856 --> 00:22:39,941
Yeah. What's up?

384
00:22:41,985 --> 00:22:43,403
Switch seats with me.

385
00:22:43,487 --> 00:22:44,488
What?

386
00:22:45,364 --> 00:22:46,365
Why?

387
00:22:46,448 --> 00:22:50,535
Because. It should be you.
You should lead the team.

388
00:22:53,121 --> 00:22:54,122
I'll follow you.

389
00:22:55,832 --> 00:23:00,504
[inspiring music playing]

390
00:23:08,387 --> 00:23:09,763
All right, Easton.

391
00:23:11,723 --> 00:23:12,891
Hands on.

392
00:23:14,810 --> 00:23:16,186
Up to shoulders.

393
00:23:23,985 --> 00:23:25,404
Walk it forward.

394
00:23:35,872 --> 00:23:39,209
Everyone, Easton's race is about to begin.
Come on over.

395
00:23:40,252 --> 00:23:42,045
I didn't think you were into rowing,

396
00:23:42,129 --> 00:23:45,173
but I suppose you must be a WAG now.
Wives and girlfriends.

397
00:23:45,257 --> 00:23:47,759
-I saw you with Perry.
-I'm neither wife nor girlfriend.

398
00:23:47,843 --> 00:23:50,387
Rumor has it neither are you.
What are you doing here?

399
00:23:51,012 --> 00:23:53,974
I'm here for my brother
and for the love of the sport.

400
00:23:54,683 --> 00:23:56,393
[Hayden] Easton, huddle up.

401
00:23:57,227 --> 00:24:00,480
First time at the Haverford in ten years.
Here's what's in front of you.

402
00:24:01,064 --> 00:24:05,152
Claremont. Haven't lost a race all year.
They'll set the pace.

403
00:24:05,235 --> 00:24:06,862
Westvale. They're beasts,

404
00:24:06,945 --> 00:24:09,781
but we've beat them before,
and we can beat them again.

405
00:24:09,865 --> 00:24:14,161
Roxbury's next to you. They're fast.
An overtake will not be easy.

406
00:24:14,828 --> 00:24:18,790
Then there's Vic City. Take them down,
and we got a chance at a medal.

407
00:24:19,291 --> 00:24:20,625
-Ready?
-[all] Easton!

408
00:24:20,709 --> 00:24:22,085
[Lana] All right, let's go.

409
00:24:27,799 --> 00:24:30,135
[Teagan] Rowing to race position.

410
00:24:33,430 --> 00:24:35,765
Wait, Cam and Teagan are both on the boat?

411
00:24:37,684 --> 00:24:40,479
[announcer] Attention all rowers
for Westvale, Claremont,

412
00:24:40,562 --> 00:24:42,814
Easton Prep, Vic City, and Roxbury.

413
00:24:42,898 --> 00:24:46,610
-Stand by.
-[Viktor] Josh in seven and Ryder in six.

414
00:24:48,111 --> 00:24:50,822
Two chances at stroke and two strikeouts.

415
00:24:50,906 --> 00:24:55,202
I thought one of you wouldn't screw it up.
Yet, here you both are.

416
00:24:58,955 --> 00:25:00,207
[announcer] Starting positions.

417
00:25:00,290 --> 00:25:01,833
[Teagan] Okay, Cam. Technique first.

418
00:25:01,917 --> 00:25:05,337
Next, 20 to sprint, then settle.
First push on my call.

419
00:25:05,420 --> 00:25:06,254
Aye-aye.

420
00:25:09,508 --> 00:25:10,675
Time to shine.

421
00:25:10,759 --> 00:25:12,677
["Set It on Fire" by ANOTR playing]

422
00:25:12,761 --> 00:25:14,221
[exhales]

423
00:25:16,264 --> 00:25:17,641
Attention…

424
00:25:19,100 --> 00:25:21,269
<i>♪ Set it on fire, I said set it ♪</i>

425
00:25:21,353 --> 00:25:22,854
-Row!
-[horn blowing]

426
00:25:23,563 --> 00:25:28,026
Three-quarter! Three-quarter!

427
00:25:28,527 --> 00:25:32,280
Full! Full!

428
00:25:32,781 --> 00:25:34,866
[cheering and yelling]

429
00:25:34,950 --> 00:25:39,579
Long and strong!

430
00:25:39,663 --> 00:25:41,039
[Hayden] We're last.

431
00:25:43,792 --> 00:25:48,213
[Teagan] Easton, don't let it get to you.
Focus on technique. Cam, keep 'em steady.

432
00:25:48,880 --> 00:25:52,300
[Claremont cox] All right,
let's take up the rate. Push!

433
00:25:54,135 --> 00:25:55,971
Claremont is off like a rocket.

434
00:25:56,054 --> 00:25:58,974
Predictable.
They've been untouchable all season.

435
00:25:59,516 --> 00:26:02,561
<i>♪ I said set it on fire</i>
<i>Set, set it on fire ♪</i>

436
00:26:02,644 --> 00:26:06,523
<i>♪ Set it on fire ♪</i>

437
00:26:06,606 --> 00:26:08,900
[Teagan] Ignore Claremont.
Stick to the plan.

438
00:26:08,984 --> 00:26:12,612
<i>♪ Set it on fire ♪</i>

439
00:26:12,696 --> 00:26:15,782
Time to bring the heat.
Westvale's in second.

440
00:26:17,492 --> 00:26:20,620
Roxbury and Vic City
are only two seats away.

441
00:26:20,704 --> 00:26:22,455
In two. One…

442
00:26:22,956 --> 00:26:24,040
Two!

443
00:26:24,124 --> 00:26:27,586
<i>♪ Set, set, I said set it on fire</i>
<i>I said set… ♪</i>

444
00:26:27,669 --> 00:26:30,088
[Roxbury cox]
Easton's on us. Roxbury, pick it up!

445
00:26:31,631 --> 00:26:35,176
[Vic City cox] Vic City.
Quick catches for five strokes.

446
00:26:35,260 --> 00:26:36,261
One.

447
00:26:36,970 --> 00:26:38,263
Two.

448
00:26:38,888 --> 00:26:39,889
-Three.
-[oarlock clatters]

449
00:26:39,973 --> 00:26:41,182
No!

450
00:26:42,100 --> 00:26:43,810
-[crowd exclaims]
-They just caught a crab.

451
00:26:43,893 --> 00:26:45,604
No way they're gonna catch up now.

452
00:26:45,687 --> 00:26:46,563
[Ella laughs]

453
00:26:47,355 --> 00:26:50,567
[feisty music playing]

454
00:26:50,650 --> 00:26:53,903
[Teagan] Four teams left,
three medals. Let's get ours!

455
00:26:53,987 --> 00:26:57,365
We are at a 34.
Cam, I need a 36 to close the gap.

456
00:26:57,449 --> 00:26:58,283
After two…

457
00:26:59,159 --> 00:27:00,368
One.

458
00:27:00,869 --> 00:27:01,786
Two!

459
00:27:01,870 --> 00:27:03,705
Punch it!

460
00:27:07,000 --> 00:27:08,793
Whoa! Whoa! We're off-balance!

461
00:27:08,877 --> 00:27:10,253
They're rushing the catch.

462
00:27:10,337 --> 00:27:13,673
Don't rush the slide, trust the rhythm.

463
00:27:15,842 --> 00:27:18,136
Josh, nice picking it up.

464
00:27:18,219 --> 00:27:19,929
Bow pair, killing it.

465
00:27:20,430 --> 00:27:22,682
Yeah! We're moving now!

466
00:27:22,766 --> 00:27:25,352
I'm on Roxbury's stern.

467
00:27:26,102 --> 00:27:31,149
Oh my God. They're closing in on Roxbury.
We have a shot at third!

468
00:27:31,232 --> 00:27:33,985
[Teagan] Easton, we can take this.
Power ten.

469
00:27:34,069 --> 00:27:37,530
-[Roxbury cox] They're passing us now!
-Now! Send it!

470
00:27:37,614 --> 00:27:41,076
-Show me what you got.
-[Roxbury cox] Keep it up. Push. Push it!

471
00:27:41,576 --> 00:27:43,495
-Do it! Come on!
-[Roxbury cox] Do it! Come on!

472
00:27:43,578 --> 00:27:46,581
-Come on, Roxbury. Two!
-[Teagan] Keep pushing. Come on!

473
00:27:46,665 --> 00:27:50,335
Yeah! Third's ours! Whoo!

474
00:27:50,418 --> 00:27:52,170
A-ha! We're in third!

475
00:27:52,253 --> 00:27:54,172
[squeals] We're in third!

476
00:27:54,255 --> 00:27:55,465
We're excited for third.

477
00:28:02,681 --> 00:28:06,476
[Teagan] Don't get cocky.
Job's not done. Keep the power up.

478
00:28:07,686 --> 00:28:08,853
[rower] Westvale!

479
00:28:08,937 --> 00:28:11,272
-They're gaining on Westvale.
-Keep the rate up, Teagan.

480
00:28:13,274 --> 00:28:17,028
Westvale's just ahead. Take it up to a 38.

481
00:28:17,112 --> 00:28:18,738
We can shut them up here.

482
00:28:18,822 --> 00:28:20,699
Pick it up! Pick it up!

483
00:28:23,743 --> 00:28:25,829
Go hard, we're moving now.

484
00:28:25,912 --> 00:28:29,332
[Westvale cox] Westvale.
We're not losing to Easton. Crank it.

485
00:28:29,416 --> 00:28:30,875
[cheering]

486
00:28:30,959 --> 00:28:33,253
Switch. Switch.

487
00:28:33,336 --> 00:28:35,505
Come on! Keep it together!

488
00:28:36,548 --> 00:28:38,883
Engine room, stay with me!

489
00:28:40,510 --> 00:28:43,012
I know it's the pain cave,
but listen to me.

490
00:28:43,096 --> 00:28:47,434
You've got a lot left in you.
Dig deep! Dig deep!

491
00:28:47,517 --> 00:28:51,688
Do it like it's your last time!
Come on. You got this!

492
00:28:53,189 --> 00:28:54,149
[cox] Drive!

493
00:28:54,232 --> 00:28:57,152
[Teagan] We're right next to them,
empty the tank!

494
00:28:57,235 --> 00:28:59,320
[cox] Push! Push!

495
00:28:59,404 --> 00:29:00,947
Go, Teagan!

496
00:29:01,030 --> 00:29:02,657
Come on, Ryder!

497
00:29:02,741 --> 00:29:04,033
Let's go, Josh!

498
00:29:04,117 --> 00:29:05,744
Go, Bronson!

499
00:29:05,827 --> 00:29:07,328
Who's Bronson?

500
00:29:07,412 --> 00:29:08,455
That's Baloo.

501
00:29:08,538 --> 00:29:11,249
Baloo is Bronson?
I thought they were two different guys.

502
00:29:12,709 --> 00:29:16,087
-Push through! Yeah! Then go!
-[cox] Push!

503
00:29:16,171 --> 00:29:17,422
-Push!
-[Teagan] Hear that?

504
00:29:17,505 --> 00:29:19,174
Claremont just finished.

505
00:29:19,257 --> 00:29:21,843
Come on, Easton. Hit these last strokes!

506
00:29:21,926 --> 00:29:25,346
-[cox] This is it! Sprint! Sprint! Sprint!
-[Teagan] Send! Send! Send!

507
00:29:25,430 --> 00:29:27,932
[all cheering and yelling]

508
00:29:28,016 --> 00:29:29,058
They did it!

509
00:29:29,142 --> 00:29:31,436
-They're in second spot.
-Okay, okay, okay, okay.

510
00:29:31,519 --> 00:29:34,522
-Power ten, guys! Let's go!
-Let's go, boys! Let's go!

511
00:29:34,606 --> 00:29:37,859
[Teagan] Come on, guys, give it your all!
You're almost there!

512
00:29:37,942 --> 00:29:41,404
-[cox] Drive!
-[Teagan] Take us home, guys. Let's go!

513
00:29:41,488 --> 00:29:42,322
Go!

514
00:29:42,405 --> 00:29:44,616
-[horn blows]
-Yeah!

515
00:29:44,699 --> 00:29:46,242
[crowd cheering]

516
00:29:46,326 --> 00:29:48,453
[all yelling and cheering]

517
00:29:48,536 --> 00:29:51,664
-Let's go! Let's go!
-Let's go!

518
00:29:51,748 --> 00:29:52,874
[all cheering]

519
00:29:52,957 --> 00:29:53,792
Oh my God!

520
00:29:55,460 --> 00:29:58,087
-Yes!
-Silver, incredible!

521
00:29:58,171 --> 00:29:59,464
Yeah!

522
00:30:00,381 --> 00:30:04,803
[victorious music playing]

523
00:30:04,886 --> 00:30:07,013
We medaled!

524
00:30:07,096 --> 00:30:08,973
[celebrating continues]

525
00:30:09,057 --> 00:30:11,226
-Whoo!
-Yeah!

526
00:30:11,768 --> 00:30:13,394
[Lana laughing]

527
00:30:16,022 --> 00:30:18,107
[laughing]

528
00:30:18,191 --> 00:30:21,277
[Teagan] Let's go! Whoo! Whoo!

529
00:30:21,361 --> 00:30:23,613
-Yes!
-Yeah!

530
00:30:23,696 --> 00:30:24,864
-Yeah!
-Whoo!

531
00:30:24,948 --> 00:30:25,990
Yeah!

532
00:30:27,867 --> 00:30:29,410
Heavier than I thought.

533
00:30:30,870 --> 00:30:32,455
Silver's pretty hypoallergenic.

534
00:30:32,956 --> 00:30:35,083
Okay, they're actually pretty cute.

535
00:30:35,166 --> 00:30:36,793
I'm never letting you go.

536
00:30:39,796 --> 00:30:42,131
-First of many.
-[team] Yeah!

537
00:30:42,715 --> 00:30:44,050
Come on!

538
00:30:44,133 --> 00:30:46,719
Yeah, not bad. Next stop, gold.

539
00:30:46,803 --> 00:30:48,429
-Yeah!
-Yeah!

540
00:30:49,889 --> 00:30:53,518
-Is this how you wanted to go out?
-It's better than I imagined.

541
00:30:54,060 --> 00:30:55,520
Here. Try it on.

542
00:30:57,772 --> 00:30:59,941
Oh, yeah. That looks pretty good to me.

543
00:31:00,024 --> 00:31:01,359
[laughing]

544
00:31:02,151 --> 00:31:05,446
-Yo! Whoa, come on, let's go!
-Whoa! What? Hey!

545
00:31:05,530 --> 00:31:07,240
[all cheering]

546
00:31:08,616 --> 00:31:11,536
Okay, wait, hold on.
Wait, where's Coach? Where's Coach?

547
00:31:11,619 --> 00:31:12,745
-Coach!
-Coach!

548
00:31:12,829 --> 00:31:14,080
-Come on!
-Come on!

549
00:31:14,163 --> 00:31:16,040
-Get in here!
-Okay.

550
00:31:16,916 --> 00:31:18,793
[Teagan] Okay. Okay, okay.

551
00:31:20,044 --> 00:31:23,548
-Okay. Eagle pride!
-[team] Eagle pride!

552
00:31:25,466 --> 00:31:26,551
[laughing]

553
00:31:31,973 --> 00:31:33,474
-Hey.
-Hey.

554
00:31:34,350 --> 00:31:35,393
Uh…

555
00:31:36,978 --> 00:31:38,563
I should have trusted you.

556
00:31:39,063 --> 00:31:41,691
And you have every right to say no, but…

557
00:31:42,191 --> 00:31:44,652
-If you ever want to hang out again…
-Just…

558
00:31:45,153 --> 00:31:46,446
[rowers murmuring] Whoa…

559
00:31:46,988 --> 00:31:48,072
[Perry laughs]

560
00:31:49,073 --> 00:31:50,533
Does that answer your question?

561
00:31:50,617 --> 00:31:52,827
[all cheering]

562
00:31:57,999 --> 00:31:59,042
Let's go.

563
00:31:59,542 --> 00:32:01,169
Cam. Can I talk to you?

564
00:32:01,252 --> 00:32:03,129
Yeah. What's up, Coach?

565
00:32:03,212 --> 00:32:04,547
I owe you an apology.

566
00:32:04,631 --> 00:32:05,632
For what?

567
00:32:05,715 --> 00:32:08,134
I told you Easton wouldn't row
for townies like us.

568
00:32:08,217 --> 00:32:11,095
I brought my own baggage into it,
and I shouldn't have.

569
00:32:11,846 --> 00:32:12,972
I was wrong.

570
00:32:13,932 --> 00:32:18,269
But I'm so glad that I was wrong
because you killed it out there today.

571
00:32:22,774 --> 00:32:24,192
I'm proud of you, man.

572
00:32:24,859 --> 00:32:25,860
Thanks, Coach.

573
00:32:30,949 --> 00:32:31,908
Ah.

574
00:32:31,991 --> 00:32:33,743
Incoming.

575
00:32:34,243 --> 00:32:37,580
Hey, it's nice to see Easton
end its losing streak.

576
00:32:37,664 --> 00:32:40,500
Silver. Not the worst.

577
00:32:40,583 --> 00:32:42,961
I'll be training in Florida
over the winter season,

578
00:32:43,044 --> 00:32:44,671
so I'll be ready for next year.

579
00:32:44,754 --> 00:32:46,130
And you, Josh?

580
00:32:49,550 --> 00:32:51,469
[tense music playing]

581
00:32:51,552 --> 00:32:53,012
Um…

582
00:32:54,847 --> 00:32:57,225
Not for me. That was my last race.

583
00:32:57,308 --> 00:32:58,184
I beg your pardon?

584
00:33:04,107 --> 00:33:05,441
I have a heart condition.

585
00:33:07,860 --> 00:33:11,322
Hypertrophic cardiomyopathy. It's serious.

586
00:33:12,365 --> 00:33:15,118
I wanted to carry on the family tradition,
but I can't.

587
00:33:16,536 --> 00:33:18,079
I'm not gonna row anymore.

588
00:33:20,623 --> 00:33:23,084
[Viktor] I'm sorry to hear that.
I wish you better health.

589
00:33:23,167 --> 00:33:26,754
Unfortunately, such a serious condition
is a risk,

590
00:33:27,630 --> 00:33:30,091
and will affect our company's plans.

591
00:33:31,592 --> 00:33:32,593
I understand.

592
00:33:34,846 --> 00:33:36,139
I don't think we heard you right…

593
00:33:38,808 --> 00:33:39,851
Dad.

594
00:33:41,269 --> 00:33:42,979
I think what you meant to say is,

595
00:33:43,062 --> 00:33:46,065
"We love you, Josh,
and we will do whatever it takes

596
00:33:46,149 --> 00:33:48,443
to get you
the best medical care possible."

597
00:33:49,777 --> 00:33:51,487
-[Viktor] Excuse me?
-[Richard] You heard me.

598
00:33:51,571 --> 00:33:54,574
Josh isn't your heir. He's my son.

599
00:33:54,657 --> 00:33:56,034
All right.

600
00:33:57,201 --> 00:34:00,747
Well, I'll let you
get back to your family time.

601
00:34:01,330 --> 00:34:02,165
Karina.

602
00:34:02,248 --> 00:34:03,374
Ryder.

603
00:34:04,000 --> 00:34:07,378
I'd love to hear more
about your winter plans.

604
00:34:12,300 --> 00:34:13,384
Sorry, man.

605
00:34:19,348 --> 00:34:21,476
-He didn't like that.
-Is that bad?

606
00:34:22,226 --> 00:34:23,227
Yes.

607
00:34:24,771 --> 00:34:25,813
But I don't care.

608
00:34:25,897 --> 00:34:27,023
[emotional music playing]

609
00:34:27,106 --> 00:34:29,817
Are you okay? Can they treat it?

610
00:34:30,943 --> 00:34:33,613
Yeah. With surgery.

611
00:34:34,864 --> 00:34:36,532
But it's a pretty rough recovery.

612
00:34:37,158 --> 00:34:38,576
We can deal with rough.

613
00:34:44,582 --> 00:34:45,625
I love you.

614
00:34:45,708 --> 00:34:46,876
I love you too, Dad.

615
00:34:48,503 --> 00:34:49,921
Let's go call your mom.

616
00:34:55,259 --> 00:34:56,886
-Hi.
-Hey.

617
00:34:56,969 --> 00:34:59,889
Congratulations! First medal in ten years.

618
00:34:59,972 --> 00:35:01,933
Yeah. The crew did good.

619
00:35:04,018 --> 00:35:05,061
Have you seen Teagan?

620
00:35:05,645 --> 00:35:07,021
Ah. Right over there.

621
00:35:07,730 --> 00:35:09,524
Is everything okay?

622
00:35:09,607 --> 00:35:10,608
I'm not sure.

623
00:35:11,818 --> 00:35:15,196
I'm sorry. My… My life is so complicated.

624
00:35:16,614 --> 00:35:18,241
Well, I'll be here when it's not.

625
00:35:26,749 --> 00:35:28,709
Hey, honey, congratulations!

626
00:35:28,793 --> 00:35:31,712
-I need to talk to you.
-Okay, well, I don't want to talk to you.

627
00:35:38,928 --> 00:35:41,681
You lied to me about Dad,
and you're keeping things from me.

628
00:35:41,764 --> 00:35:44,934
Yes. He's here,
and I'm hiding him from the FBI.

629
00:35:45,017 --> 00:35:46,644
What? Mom!

630
00:35:46,727 --> 00:35:48,896
This is why
I don't want to tell you things.

631
00:35:48,980 --> 00:35:51,357
Okay, what do we do?
Are we gonna get in trouble?

632
00:35:51,440 --> 00:35:53,860
-[Ella] How bad is aiding and abetting?
-[Teagan] Pretty bad!

633
00:35:53,943 --> 00:35:55,903
Well, whatever, honey.
We'll figure it out.

634
00:35:57,029 --> 00:35:59,157
Teag, you were incredible out there.

635
00:35:59,240 --> 00:36:01,075
Dad, okay, you can't be here.

636
00:36:01,159 --> 00:36:03,119
You gotta go. What if somebody sees you?

637
00:36:03,202 --> 00:36:04,704
Maybe it's time they do.

638
00:36:04,787 --> 00:36:07,206
I don't want you to wonder
where I am anymore.

639
00:36:07,290 --> 00:36:09,375
I'm going to turn myself in.

640
00:36:13,337 --> 00:36:14,338
You're sure?

641
00:36:15,256 --> 00:36:16,257
I'm sure.

642
00:36:18,009 --> 00:36:20,261
Listen, Teag,
I know you're upset at your mom,

643
00:36:20,344 --> 00:36:22,889
but she was just protecting you
from my mess.

644
00:36:22,972 --> 00:36:27,059
She's built a great life for you,
and she did it with less than nothing.

645
00:36:27,560 --> 00:36:29,228
She's pretty amazing.

646
00:36:33,774 --> 00:36:36,527
-[agent] Got eyes on the suspect.
-It's time to go.

647
00:36:39,113 --> 00:36:40,072
[Ella sighs]

648
00:36:42,408 --> 00:36:44,535
[agent] Mr. Tao. You need to come with us.

649
00:36:52,210 --> 00:36:53,961
Exciting day for Easton.

650
00:36:54,045 --> 00:36:56,172
Hey, we got on the podium,
just like you wanted.

651
00:36:56,255 --> 00:36:57,340
Yes.

652
00:36:58,674 --> 00:37:02,970
I couldn't help but notice
that both Teagan and Cam were in the boat.

653
00:37:04,680 --> 00:37:07,975
Were you not able to find out
who the responsible party was?

654
00:37:09,435 --> 00:37:10,645
I was.

655
00:37:10,728 --> 00:37:12,772
But ultimately, as head coach of the team,

656
00:37:12,855 --> 00:37:17,401
I decided that the responsibility
for their actions lies with me.

657
00:37:17,485 --> 00:37:18,778
I see.

658
00:37:19,946 --> 00:37:22,198
Then I don't have much choice,
Coach Hayden.

659
00:37:23,574 --> 00:37:24,700
You're fired.

660
00:37:24,784 --> 00:37:27,703
[somber music playing]

661
00:37:34,794 --> 00:37:36,254
-Hey.
-Hey.

662
00:37:36,337 --> 00:37:38,506
I heard about your dad. You okay?

663
00:37:40,007 --> 00:37:41,217
No.

664
00:37:42,802 --> 00:37:46,806
But, uh… you know,
me and my mom will figure it out.

665
00:37:48,140 --> 00:37:49,809
How'd things go with your family?

666
00:37:49,892 --> 00:37:51,686
Surprisingly not terrible.

667
00:37:52,728 --> 00:37:54,522
Though we might be poor soon.

668
00:37:55,564 --> 00:37:56,941
Poor for us.

669
00:37:57,858 --> 00:38:00,695
Feel free to hit me up for tips
on surviving your downfall.

670
00:38:00,778 --> 00:38:02,029
Will do.

671
00:38:02,113 --> 00:38:02,947
[laughs]

672
00:38:04,907 --> 00:38:06,158
["Syncing" by Miss Grit playing]

673
00:38:06,242 --> 00:38:07,368
Listen.

674
00:38:08,536 --> 00:38:11,080
It's been a really hard time,
and you've been there for me.

675
00:38:12,206 --> 00:38:14,333
You've seen me at my worst.

676
00:38:14,417 --> 00:38:16,752
-Yeah, daily.
-Yeah, well…

677
00:38:16,836 --> 00:38:18,713
You've never seen me at my best.

678
00:38:19,213 --> 00:38:20,214
I'm working on it.

679
00:38:20,923 --> 00:38:22,717
What, you're building a better Josh?

680
00:38:23,884 --> 00:38:27,847
Yeah. And I'm hoping
when you meet that guy,

681
00:38:29,265 --> 00:38:30,766
you'll give him a second chance.

682
00:38:32,643 --> 00:38:33,894
Okay.

683
00:38:36,397 --> 00:38:39,942
See you around.
If I don't die on the operating table.

684
00:38:40,026 --> 00:38:41,193
[Josh laughs]

685
00:38:46,490 --> 00:38:53,205
<i>♪ But nothing stayed</i>
<i>Right where I left it ♪</i>

686
00:39:00,004 --> 00:39:02,340
<i>♪ I'm starting to move… ♪</i>

687
00:39:02,423 --> 00:39:04,592
Just a few more loads.

688
00:39:06,927 --> 00:39:08,679
What should we do with the straw hats?

689
00:39:08,763 --> 00:39:11,015
-Burn them?
-Thanks for today.

690
00:39:11,098 --> 00:39:13,142
What are you gonna do
with the money from this party?

691
00:39:13,225 --> 00:39:14,894
Pay Teagan's tuition.

692
00:39:14,977 --> 00:39:17,521
Okay, after that boring thing,

693
00:39:18,022 --> 00:39:20,816
you should think about
what you wanna do for yourself.

694
00:39:20,900 --> 00:39:22,401
Be selfish.

695
00:39:23,486 --> 00:39:24,779
You're a good kid. You know that?

696
00:39:26,155 --> 00:39:28,574
What an awful thing to say to someone.

697
00:39:30,493 --> 00:39:32,495
[song continues]

698
00:39:40,920 --> 00:39:42,171
[woman] Juliet.

699
00:39:46,425 --> 00:39:47,426
Mom?

700
00:39:54,725 --> 00:39:55,935
Hey, Coxie.

701
00:39:56,435 --> 00:39:58,396
Hey, stroke seat.

702
00:39:58,479 --> 00:40:00,523
["Focus Is Power" by Self Esteem playing]

703
00:40:00,606 --> 00:40:01,816
Been a day.

704
00:40:03,234 --> 00:40:05,403
Yeah, certainly has.

705
00:40:06,445 --> 00:40:08,614
Can't say I imagined this
when you hit me with your bike.

706
00:40:09,907 --> 00:40:11,367
You hit me.

707
00:40:14,995 --> 00:40:17,331
<i>♪ Don't be too loud or too quiet ♪</i>

708
00:40:17,915 --> 00:40:19,834
<i>♪ But I got all this fight ♪</i>

709
00:40:19,917 --> 00:40:25,339
<i>♪ And now I see it clear</i>
<i>With every passing of each year ♪</i>

710
00:40:25,423 --> 00:40:28,259
<i>♪ I deserve to be here ♪</i>

711
00:40:32,513 --> 00:40:35,099
[Lana] Hey, Teagan, are you in here?
I wanna talk to you.

712
00:40:35,599 --> 00:40:38,185
Yeah, I am over here.

713
00:40:38,811 --> 00:40:40,062
-[Cam] I'll go.
-Okay.

714
00:40:44,150 --> 00:40:45,359
Night, Coach.

715
00:40:47,194 --> 00:40:48,195
[Teagan] What's up?

716
00:40:49,029 --> 00:40:52,491
Do you hear that?
It's the sound of your wish coming true.

717
00:40:53,075 --> 00:40:55,744
-My wish?
-I spoke to Cabrera this morning.

718
00:40:55,828 --> 00:40:59,165
Apparently there's a group of girls that
have shown interest in a girls' team,

719
00:40:59,248 --> 00:41:01,917
and they're backed by a wealthy donor.

720
00:41:02,001 --> 00:41:05,045
Congrats, Teagan.
Come spring, you're back in a boat.

721
00:41:06,505 --> 00:41:09,300
What? Oh my God, that's so amazing.

722
00:41:09,383 --> 00:41:12,761
-Thank you so much. I--
-Hey, don't thank me.

723
00:41:12,845 --> 00:41:14,138
Thank the Garner Foundation.

724
00:41:14,221 --> 00:41:17,683
["Fade Away" by Girl Tones playing]

725
00:41:17,766 --> 00:41:18,809
What?

726
00:41:20,811 --> 00:41:21,812
Hey, babe.

727
00:41:24,690 --> 00:41:27,318
I can't wait to be crewmates.

728
00:41:28,235 --> 00:41:31,655
It looks like you row for me now.

729
00:41:33,866 --> 00:41:35,326
<i>♪ Fade ♪</i>

730
00:41:38,245 --> 00:41:40,956
<i>♪ Away ♪</i>

731
00:41:43,584 --> 00:41:45,586
<i>♪ Fade ♪</i>

732
00:41:48,005 --> 00:41:52,635
<i>♪ Altercation</i>
<i>No motivation ♪</i>

733
00:41:53,844 --> 00:41:57,556
<i>♪ Oh no, it's too complicated ♪</i>

734
00:41:58,057 --> 00:42:02,311
<i>♪ I'm jaded</i>
<i>I'm so frustrated ♪</i>

735
00:42:02,394 --> 00:42:04,939
<i>♪ I'm losing my patience ♪</i>

736
00:42:07,316 --> 00:42:11,654
<i>♪ You always seem to bother me ♪</i>

737
00:42:12,530 --> 00:42:16,534
<i>♪ You deny your immaturity ♪</i>

738
00:42:16,617 --> 00:42:21,205
<i>♪ And as the waves build and break ♪</i>

739
00:42:21,288 --> 00:42:25,584
<i>♪ I'm owed an apology ♪</i>

740
00:42:25,668 --> 00:42:28,045
<i>♪ Fade ♪</i>

741
00:42:30,089 --> 00:42:33,384
<i>♪ Away ♪</i>

742
00:42:33,467 --> 00:42:35,469
[song ends]
